<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">11 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 11 April, from 1241 to 1970.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hungary" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hungary.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1241 <span class="tih-ago">785 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mongols destroy the Hungarian army at Mohi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Mongol forces under Batu and Subutai encircled and annihilated King Béla IV's army by the Sajó river. Hungary was laid open to a year of devastating occupation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/mongol-empire">Mongol Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subutai">Subutai</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1689 <span class="tih-ago">337 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William III and Mary II are crowned joint monarchs</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">William and Mary were crowned together in Westminster Abbey after accepting the Declaration of Rights. The settlement confirmed the Glorious Revolution and the limits Parliament had placed on the Crown.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/napoleon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1814 <span class="tih-ago">212 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of Fontainebleau sends Napoleon to Elba</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The allied powers signed the treaty confirming Napoleon's abdication and granting him the island of Elba as a sovereign principality. He escaped less than a year later for the Hundred Days.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1945 <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US troops reach Buchenwald concentration camp</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">American soldiers arrived at Buchenwald near Weimar, where prisoners had already taken control of the camp. Some 56,000 people had died there; Eisenhower later had local Germans brought to see it.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1961 <span class="tih-ago">65 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Adolf Eichmann's trial opens in Jerusalem</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Adolf Eichmann, a principal organiser of the deportation of Europe's Jews, went on trial in Jerusalem. Survivor testimony broadcast worldwide shaped public understanding of the Holocaust; he was hanged in 1962.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1970 <span class="tih-ago">56 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Apollo 13 lifts off for the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Apollo 13 launched from Kennedy Space Center. Two days out an oxygen tank exploded, the lunar landing was abandoned, and the crew used the lunar module as a lifeboat to return safely.</p></div></li></ol>
